<title>SPAIN: Repsol meets SEPI to discuss share offer.</title>
<headline>Repsol meets SEPI to discuss share offer.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Spain's Repsol is to meet today with the chairman of state holding company SEPI to discuss the placement of the government's remaining 10 percent in the petrochemical company, a SEPI official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The meeting is one of many that the SEPI chairman is holding with the chairmen of public companies and I am sure they will discuss the privatisation, although it will not be the main topic of conversation,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>In principle, Spain is due to sell its Repsol stake in spring 1997.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2160</p>
